      "id": "lean-startup-s075-p00914",
      "source_en": "Charles E. Duryea, himself a pioneer carmaker, revealed that from 1900 to 1908, 501 companies were formed in the United States for the purpose of manufacturing automobiles. Sixty percent of them folded outright within a couple of years; another 6 percent moved into other areas of production.” This quote is from the Ford biography The People’s Tycoon: Henry Ford and the American Century by Steven Watts (New York: Vintage, 2006).",
